In Brazil, the air quality standards (AQS) were updated by
the National Environment Council (CONAMA) with the
CONAMA Resolution n° 491/2018, revised for the first time
after more than two decades. The new Resolution establishes
intermediary air quality standards (IS) to be progressively
reached along the years aiming at a final standard (FS) based
on WHO guidelines. This methodology has already been
employed by the states of São Paulo and Espírito Santo,
