COPD, and individuals with stable coronary disease 
revealed that, in all participants, walking for 2 h in a 
park led to an increase in lung function, an increase 
that was absent or reduced after walking along a busy 
traffic street.
(59)
  Studies  in  humans
(59)
  and  studies  
using  mathematical  models
(64,65)
  have  shown  that,  
for healthy individuals and even for individuals with 
chronic diseases, mild-to-moderate exercise in polluted 
environments, even where pollution levels are above 
the reference values recommended by the WHO,
(7)
 has 
beneficial effects that override the effects of inhalation 
of an increased load of pollutants. Therefore, the 
balance  of  studies  suggests  that  mild-to-moderate  
exercise is beneficial even in polluted places.
(8,60,64,65)
Other pulmonary conditions
