B. Requirements
The first requirement involves determining the number and
types  of  pollutants  be  evaluated  in  air  quality  monitoring.
Selecting  the  type  of  pollutants  is  highly  related  to  agency
specific  requirements,  sources  and  materials  of  emitting  bad
air; while, the number is closely related to coverage, accuracy,
cost,  reliability,  and  efficiency.  In  general,  the  decision  is
highly dependent on the agency specific requirements, appli-
cation  location  (e.g.,  indoor or  outdoor and  place  of  indoor)
and  sources  of  emitting  bad  air.  For  example,  we  can  adopt
the  six  pollutants,  CO,  O
