of  the  day,  considering  the  colour  temperature  range  of  the  
smart  bulb.  The  smart  light’s  colour  temperature variance 
throughout the day depends on the period of the day.  
The WSN coordinator computation platform (Raspberry   Pi) 
is  also  responsible  for  sending  the acquired  data  to  an  online  
database. Firebase Realtime Database is used for that purpose, 
due to its ease  of  access  and  available  APIs.  In order to write 
data  in  the  database, a  Python  interface  is  used  with  the 
Firebase’s  REST  API.  To  make  sure  the  sensor  readings  are  
always  available,  that  same  data  is  also  saved  locally  on  the  
Raspberry’s SD card, on a LibreOffice calc spreadsheet. 
As  for  the  web  application,  it  is  designed  to  monitor  the  
indoor  air  quality  in  real-time and warn  the  user  if  indoor  air  
