environments are also presented and discussed. Finally, we present the major studies on 
the subject conducted in Brazil. Health care and disease prevention services should be 
aware of this important risk factor in order to counsel more susceptible individuals about 
protective measures that can facilitate their treatment, as well as promoting the adoption 
of environmental measures that contribute to the reduction of such emissions.
Keywords: Air  pollution;  Particulate  matter;  Respiratory  tract  diseases;  Pulmonary  
disease, chronic obstructive; Asthma; Respiratory tract infections; Lung neoplasms.
