9726,0.010900111]'), ('26251e88-cadc-469e-9bda-a5203757c24d', 'A. Hardware 
Each  sensor  node  (Node  1-  4)  consists  of  multiple  sensors  
and a microcontroller:  Node 1 is  formed  by  a  temperature and 
relative   humidity   sensor,   a   light   intensity   sensor   (Light 
Dependent   Resistor   (LDR)) and   an   electret   microphone   
amplifier. 
 For  the  temperature  and  relative humidity measurements, 
the  Si7021  solid  state  sensor  from  Silicon  Labs  was  used.   It 
performs analog-to-digital conversions, signal processing, data 
calibration and it   has an I
2
C communication interface. It has low 
power     consumption     and     performs     relative     humidity     
measurements, with ±3% accuracy and a measurement range of 
0-80% RH, and temperature measurements accuracy of ±0.4ºC 
for  a  10ºC  to  85ºC  measurement  range  [11]. Due  to  its  high  
accuracy and low power consumption, this sensor was chosen 
to measure the indoor thermal comfort during daily activities.', '{"loc":{"lines":{"to":240,"from":223}},"pdf":{"info":{"Title":"Indoor Air Quality Monitoring System to Prevent the Triggering of Respiratory Distress","Creator":"Appligent StampPDF Batch 6.5","ModDate":"D:20200319162341-04''00''","Subject":"2019 International Conference on Sensing and Instrumentation in IoT Era (ISSI);2019; ; ; ","Producer":"Adobe PDF Library 19.12.66; modified using iText® 7.1.1 ©2000-2018 iText Group NV (AGPL-version)","CreationDate":"D:20190803163143+01''00''","IsXFAPresent":false,"PDFFormatVersion":"1.4","IsAcroFormPresent":false},"version":"1.10.100","metadata":{"_metadata":{"dc:title":"Indoor Air Quality Monitoring System to Prevent the Triggering of Respiratory Distress","dc:format":"application/pdf","dc:creator":"Mariana Jacob RodriguesOctavian PostolacheFrancisco Cercas","dc:subject":"indoor air qualityindoor lighting qualityenvironmental medicinerespiratory impairmentwireless sensor network (WSN)internet of things (IoT)web application","dc:publisher":"IEEE","dc:description":"2019 International Conference on Sensing and Instrumentation in IoT Era (ISSI);2019; ; ;","prism:endingpage":"6","prism:startingpage":"1","prism:publicationname":"2019 International Conference on Sensing and Instrumentation in IoT Era (ISSI)","prism:coverdisplaydate":"Aug. 2019"}},"totalPages":6},"source":"blob","blobType":"application/pdf"}', '[0.0123632,-0.008144755,-0.016850412,-0.03729994,0.0223192,0.008022058,0.012258031,-0.03655207,0.02092863,0.007244976,0.0052876635,0.026222138,-0.024095386,-0.0037802414,-0.011872412,0.008448577,0.027297199,0.020414472,-0.022097176,0.019900313,0.020554697,0.018182551,0.03024193,-0.04209097,0.004609908,-0.031457216,0.032205086,0.007992844,0.010937576,-0.03935658,0.0043615922,-0.016090857,-0.020180764,0.007642281,-0.046134137,0.050247412,-0.030125076,0.01575198,-0.011860726,0.008460262,-0.02993811,0.029564176,-0.043469854,0.00048640664,-0.0297044,-0.07240301,-0.0542