For O
3
, it can be observed in Fig.5that the final standard
(MDA8 100μgm
−3
) was exceeded in all 3 years in São Paulo
(114 exceedances). This pollutant has already been identified
as attention point by Environmental Company of the state of
São Paulo (CETESB2018) due to the high levels of emissions
of ozone precursors, especially from vehicular sources. In
Vitória, no exceedances were recorded, but 34% of the data
for 2016 was not available, during the final days of August
and the end of December, when there are favorable conditions
to ozone formation (spring and initial of summer). Only six
exceedances were recorded in Belo Horizonte in 2015 and one
in 2017. Exceedances were not found in Rio de Janeiro in
2015 and 2016, but O
3
concentrations were higher in 2017,
registering 19 exceedances and the highest concentration for
all cities (245.3μgm
−3
), in the beginning of spring.
