major stream of research in wireless sensor network [30], [31],
in which protocol standard has been developed.
The fourth requirement includes the needs of periodic cal-
ibration. Most sensors are susceptible to drift error or impact
by environmental changes. Drift is the gradual deviation of a
sensor’s  readings  from  the  correct  value  for  long  term.  This
problem  is  likely  caused  by  material  degradation,  exposure
to  sulfur  compounds  or  acids,  aging,  or  condensate  on  the
sensor  surface  etc.  [32], [33]. The  problem can  be  corrected
by   periodic  calibration,  which   can   be  done  with   regular
maintenance  or  automatic  software  compensation  [32],  [33].
The  deviation  caused  by  environmental  change  is  more  or
less  a short term effect, which can  be calibrated by dynamic
