stored  on  the  database),  a  humidifier  to  increase  humidity  
(moisture)  levels,  and  finally  a  single-room ventilation unit to  
displace   indoor   pollutants, increase   thermal   comfort   or   
dehumidify  the  environment.  Then, a  unique  web  application  
developed for this purpose is used to analyse the recorded data, 
to give the user  manual control over the smart lighting system 
and  other  actuators, to allow the user to modify the threshold 
values related to asthma, and to implement an additional alert 
mechanism.  The application works on multiple platforms and it 
is   compatible   with   the most   common   operating   systems,   
enabling it to be used by anyone through its personal computer, 
laptop, tablet or smartphone.
 
