4. Conclusions
In this study,relationships between AAQand respiratoryhealthof
the participants residing in three different towns of Çanakkale city,
Turkey were assessed between August 2013 and 2014. AQ measure-
mentsandAQMSsdatafornon-measuredAAQparameterswereusedin
this study. To estimate the proportions of the emission sources in the
region, an emission inventory was also prepared in the region and
AERMODmodellingsystemwasappliedfortheyearof2013.According
toemissioninventoryandAQmodellingstudyresults,theindustrywas
the most polluting sector for NOx and SO
2
, while road traffic and re-
sidentialheatingwerethemostpollutingsectorsforCOandPM
10
.SO
2
emissions were mainly coming from thermal power plants and low-
quality coal (high sulfur and ash content) use for domestic heating in
the region. In winter season, PM
10
and CO emissions were mainly
