resolution. Locationsof thepollution sources andmodel domain were
illustrated inFig. 1. Seven point sources including industrial facilities
and thermal power plants and 409 area sources including residential
heating and traffic sector were determined as input of the AERMOD
modelling system. All concentrations were predicted for the year of
2013.
The model performance was tested by comparing the predicted
pollutant concentrations with those measured at two ambient air
qualitymonitoringstations(CenterandÇanAQMSs).Severalmethods
such as root of the mean square error (RMSE), correlation coefficient
(R)andtheindexofagreement(d)wereused.Theindexofagreement
determines the degree towhich magnitudes and signs ofthe observed
value about mean are related to the predicted deviation about mean
predicted value, and allows for sensitivity toward difference in ob-
