2
gas  190  ppm.  Figure  7  and  Algorithm  2  depict  the
illustrative  process  of  determining  sensor  result  using  cross
sensitivity table.
C. Calibration With Temperature and Humidity Dependency
Thick  film  metal-oxide  semiconductor  sensors  are  often
affected by temperature and humidity [16], [17]. For example,
Table  IX  shows  the  resistance  ratios  (Rs/Ro)  values  under
the  same  conditions  for  Figaro  gas  sensors  [27].  Thus,  pre-
calibrated  data  needs  to  be  adjusted  periodically  (or  called
running  calibration)  based  on  the  temperature  and  humidity
dependency table to ensure sensing accuracy.
