b-9c9b-4bd5969d0bc4', '4238IEEE SENSORS JOURNAL, VOL. 14, NO. 12, DECEMBER 2014
Algorithm 1An Algorithm for Smoothing Sensor Data
Rs (Sensor resistor)
Ro(Output load resistor)
Rs/Ro (Sensor resistance ratio)
1:ifRs/Ro≥±3σ(Rs/Ro)
2:thenFilter out
3:elseKeep Rs/Ro
4:end if
A. Smoothing Algorithm
It  is  common  for  sensors  in  an  array  generate  suddenly
temporary errors in electrical errors such as out of control. This
kind of error comes up suddenly and disappeared. Ni et al. [34]
defined the  outlier as,  “those measurements that significantly
deviate  from  the  normal  pattern  of  sensed  data”.  Outliers
need  to  be  detected  and  remove  to  get  accurate  measures.
A  smoothing  algorithm  is  introduced  for  filtering  out  noise.
To  smooth  gas  sensor  data,  we  capture  important  trends  in
repeated  statistical  survey  and  standard  deviation  with±3σ
is  used  for  limitation.  Algorithm  1  illustrates  the  smoothing
process.
