10
was linked to an approximately 13% increase
in odds of symptomatic decreases in PEF and a similar increase
in odds of dyspnea(46). In addition, in another study of 40 sub-
jects with COPD, daily increases in PM
10
concentrations were
associated with night time chest symptoms and increases in NO
2
concentrations were associated with increased rescue medica-
tion use(43).
