cardiovascular diseases were not investigated in the present
study because the scarcity number of epidemiological studies
regarding this outcome for the four cities, which not support a
reliable analysis of the benefits related to an improvement in
air quality for this outcome.
Methodology
The analysis of public health benefits due to the air pollution
reduction considered the four state capitals in the Southeast of
Brazil: São Paulo (São Paulo state) Rio de Janeiro (Rio de
Janeiro state), Vitória (Espírito Santo state) and Belo
Horizonte (Minas Gerais state), according to Fig.1.
To estimate avoided hospital admissions, the log-normal
concentration-response function (Eq. 1) was used, based on
Sacks et al. (2018).
