2.5
monitoring in Rio de Janeiro is
performed manually every 6 days, which explains the fewer data
points. It had 58 monitoring data points in 2015, 59 in 2016, and
52 in 2017, accounting for 16% of the days of the year in the first
2 years and 14% of 2017. The city only presented two
exceedances in the years of analysis, which corroborates findings
of authors such as Godoy et al. (2009), who had already
Fig. 2Number of hospital
admissions of children (< 5 years
old) and the elderly (> 64 years
old) due to respiratory diseases
for the four cities and investigated
years
