conditions are critical to the user. Indoor’s thermal comfort, air 
quality and lighting quality are changed and improved through 
the implementation of actuator nodes, automatically controlled 
by  the  coordinator  node.  A  web-based  application  providing 
full remote control over the system and real-time monitoring of 
the environment is also presented. 
III. SYSTEM DESCRIPTION 
In order to create an indoor air quality measuring system that 
envisions  to  reduce  the  risk  of  asthma  attacks  and  COPD  by 
monitoring  respiratory  distress  triggering  factors,   a  wireless 
sensor  network  with  multiple  measuring  nodes,  a  real-time 
database, a set of actuators and a  web  application for the end-
user  was  considered.  To  improve  the  indoor  environmental  
quality    (IEQ) levels,    a    smart    light    system    was    also    
