In the first stage of ÇanakkaleHealthAir project, a detailed ques-
tionnairewascompletedbyover1000adultparticipants(age≥18)and
theresultsofthispartofthestudyarealreadygiveninMenteseetal.
(2018). This present article covers the second stage of the project. A
sub-group among the volunteered participants of the first stage of the
study were randomly selected as participants of the present study.
These participants completed another short questionnaire by face-to-
face interviews on a seasonal basis. The questionnaire composed of
questions regarding participants’ socio-demographic characteristics,
general and respiratory health conditions as well as prevalence of
chronicrespiratorysymptoms,andenvironmentalconditions.Thefinal
number of the participants whom attended the monthly respiratory
function test were more than 90% of the study year, defined as the
