Diagnostic of the air quality and its human
health effects
Air quality monitoring data
It is known that some monitoring stations are usually more
sensitive to relevant air pollution sources than others (Andrade
et al.2017). Vitória is an example, where a significant varia-
tion was observed between pollutant concentration obtained
in different monitoring stations. Thus, a spatially averaged
concentration may not necessarily represent real air quality
in a smaller scale.
Figure3presents 24-h PM
10
averages for the four cities within
