Epidemiological studies indicate that cardiovascular and respiratory
systems are primarily affected systems from the air pollution. Gen-
erally, effects of air pollution on human health is accomplished by
mortality and morbidity ratios by hospital records (WHO, 2014). A
large number of epidemiological studies have shown that daily fluc-
tuation of air pollution is linked with the daily number of deaths,
mainly from cardiovascular and respiratory diseases (Samoli et al.,
2008).Dailyvariationindiseaseburdenduetourbanpollutionresults
