36
 PM was the focus 
of these studies, but gaseous criteria air pollutants were often 
included  for  their  independent  effects  or  interaction  with 
and modification of PM effect. PM size evaluation evolved 
from TSP to PM
10
 and then to PM
2.5
. Earlier studies mostly 
focused on a single city, and many evaluated total mortality 
or mortality due to cardiorespiratory diseases or respiratory 
diseases,
50–56
