small  size  living  room, a  medium  size  classroom,  and  a  big
church – to illustrate the overall functionality of the prototype
system,  the  factors  impact  air  quality,  the  needs  and  effects
of data smoothing, calibration and aggregation. The prototype
monitor system that we constructed has four gas sensors built
in  and  has  an  expansion  socket  to  add  additional  sensors.
The  system  was  developed to  closely  monitor the  indoor air
quality level according to US EPA air quality standard (Note:
The  standard  can  be  changed  according  to  different  regions/
countries requirements). To  measure power consumption, we
use  the  EZ  GP4303D  power  supply  device,  configured  to
provide  5V  to  each  sensor  node.  The  EDM-4750  digital
multimeter  (DMM)  is  then  used  to  measure the  current flow
