170
 with 467,994 residents aged 45–85 years without 
COPD had a 5-year exposure period and a 4-year follow-up 
period. The 5-year average concentrations were 4.10 μg/m
3 
for PM
2.5 
and 32.2 μg/m
3 
(or 17 ppb) for NO
2
. In unadjusted 
single-pollutant models, PM
2.5
, NO
2
, and NO were associ-
ated  with  COPD  hospitalization  and  mortality,  although 
after  adjustment  for  covariates,  these  air  pollutants  were 
not significantly associated with COPD hospitalization and 
mortality.
