f-4043-a22d-438cead5a289', 'mo nitoring system that measures the levels of pollutants present 
in the air, as well as the temperature and humidity levels in r
ea  l-
time. A smart lighting system will also be implemented to adapt 
both the level and the colour of indoor lighting throughout the 
day, as well as alerting the user when the air-quality parameters 
exceed  an  imposed  threshold  value.  In  order  to  provide  data  
analysis, system control and an additional alert mechanism, a 
unique web application called “Saga” was also developed. 
This  paper  is  organized  as  fo llows:  Section  II  presents  the  
literature  review,  followed  by  Section  III,  where  the  system’s 
description of the hardware and software is made. The obtained 
results are presented and discussed in Section IV, followed by 
Section V that summarises conclusio ns   and future work. 
