relationship between air pollutants and cardiovascular
diseases. Besides respiratory diseases, Ferreira et al. (2016)
also investigated circulatory diseases, with the RR percentage
being smaller for PM
10
in elderly for this outcome, 2.7% (CI
−2.2%–7.9%), against 12.8% (CI 6.0–20.0) for respiratory
diseases. Considering PM
10
