have demonstrated that heat exposure is associated with respira-
tory morbidity. A study in New York City found that the risk of
COPD hospitalization increased by 7.6% for every 1°Cincrease
above a threshold temperature of 29°C(87). Studies have used
Medicare data to provide estimates of effect that are represen-
tative of a broader portion of the U.S. population (88,89). In a
study that included 12.5 million elderly individuals in 213 urban
U.S. counties, there was a 4.7% increased risk of hospitalization
for COPD for every 10 degree F increase in ambient tempera-
ture(88). Residents of more temperate climates are more likely
to be adversely impacted by the effects of extreme heat exposure
and access to air condition has been identified as a strong pro-
tective factor (81,84,90). The mechanisms by which heat expo-
sure adversely impacts COPD are not entirely understood. In', '{"loc":{"lines":{"to":513,"from":499}},"pdf":{"info":{"Title":"The Effects of Air Pollution and Temperature on COPD","Author":"Nadia N. Hansel","Creator":"LaTeX with hyperref package","ModDate":"D:20160415172439+05''30''","Subject":"COPD: Journal of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, 2015. doi:10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","Keywords":"COPD,heat,nitrogen dioxide,ozone,particulate matter","Producer":"Acrobat Distiller 10.1.10 (Windows)","CreationDate":"D:20160415172420+05''30''","IsXFAPresent":false,"PDFFormatVersion":"1.4","IsAcroFormPresent":false},"version":"1.10.100","metadata":{"_metadata":{"dc:lang":"en","dc:title":"The Effects of Air Pollution and Temperature on COPD","pdfx:doi":"10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","dc:format":"application/pdf","prism:doi":"10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","prism:url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","dc:creator":"Nadia N. HanselMeredith C. McCormackVictor Kim","dc:subject":"COPDheatnitrogen dioxideozoneparticulate matter","prism:issn":"1541-2555","prism:eissn":"1541-2563","dc:publisher":"Taylor & Francis","pdf:keywords":"COPD,heat,nitrogen dioxide,ozone,particulate matter","pdf:producer":"Acrobat Distiller 10.1.10 (Windows)","prism:number":"3","prism:volume":"13","crossmark:doi":"10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","dc:identifier":"10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","dc:description":"COPD: Journal of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, 2015. doi:10.3109/15412555.2015.1089846","xmp:createdate":"2016-04-15T17:24:20+05:30","xmp:modifydate":"2016-04-15T17:24:39+05:30","prism:copyright":"Copyright 2016 Taylor & Francis","prism:issuename":"","xmp:creatortool":"LaTeX with hyperref package","prism:endingpage":"379","xmp:metadatadate":"2016-04-15T17:24:39+05:30","prism:startingpage":"372","pdfx:crossmarkdomains":"www.tandfonline.com","prism:aggregationtype":"Journal","prism:publicationname":"COPD: Journal of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease","crossmark:crossma