(62)
 A study 
conducted in London, United Kingdom,
(63)
 compared 
changes  over  time  in  lung  function  and  sputum  
inflammatory markers in adults with asthma who 
walked for 2 h in a park and, on a separate occasion, 
along a busy traffic street. Participants with asthma 
showed a significant decline in lung function and an 
increase in inflammatory markers after walking along 
a busy traffic street.
