Index   Terms— Air   quality   monitoring,   calibration,   energy
consumption, indoor, wireless  sensor  network.
I.  INTRODUCTION
A
IR quality is one of the important measures to be closely
monitored  in  real-time  for  today’s  urban  ecosystems,
because air  quality has major influence on the  health, safety,
productivity  and  comfort  of  people  [1]–[3].  With  growing
transportation and population density, increasing global warm-
ing  and  sudden  climate  change,  the  air  quality  in  many  big
cities  worldwide  have  frequently  below  the  environmental
quality standards [4]–[7]. Many countries have developed their
own infrastructure, methodology and standards to monitor and
provide alert to their citizen. For example, the Environmental
