Abstract— In  this  paper,   an  indoor  air  quality  monitoring  
system based on a wireless sensor network (WSN) and compatible 
with  the internet  of  things  (IoT)  is  presented.  By  providing 
relevant information about indoor air conditions,  the system may 
help to prevent the triggering of respiratory distresses, such as an 
asthma crisis, by  highlighting critical air quality conditions. The 
sensor network contains several sensing nodes with  temperature, 
