2
(IEMA,2019), and higher concentrations are observed in mon-
itoring station more sensible to emissions from such industries
(mainly due to the characteristic wind direction in the region). As
for Belo Horizonte, peak concentrations occurred in 2015, from
May 27th to June 6th, with a maximum concentration of
53.1μgm
−3
and an annual average of 4.0μgm
−3
.Thesepeaks
were recorded by an automatic monitoring station located in
Amazonas Avenue, the main avenue of the Metropolitan
Region of Belo Horizonte. Santos (2018) showed that approxi-
mately 76% of SO
2
emissions in Belo Horizonte are from vehic-
ular sources.
Regarding CO, all 8-h moving average concentrations in the
four cities were found below the CONAMA Resolution 491/
2018 standard (9 ppm) during the respective years of study.
