ty based on the
US EPA’s AQI. Continuous visualized bars based on different
color and size that indicates current air quality trend provides
easier information.
V.   I
NFORMATIONPROCESSING
Information   processing,   which   involves   the   process   of
extracting  useful  and  timely  information  from  the  captured
data  to  support  decision  making,  is  the  cornerstone  of  any
effective smart sensing applications. Figure 6 shows the com-
mon information processing tasks of sensor network: (1) data
smoothing, in  which  a  smoothing  algorithm is  introduced to
prevent  from  sensor  errors;  (2)  data  calibration,  in  which
temperature/humidity dependency and sensor cross sensitivity
tables are used to calibrate the data captured from various gas
sensors;  and  (3)  data  aggregation,  in  which  an  aggregation
